# Sponsors

## Zetaris

The only door to data. Every runtime read is federated SQL through
Zetaris: the local Docker install on the 5080 PC, never the AWS cluster
route. Postgres plus PostGIS registers as a JDBC datasource; point in
polygon runs in PostGIS. The USL model `porch_light_usl` declares entities
and relationships; DQ rules feed the "couldn't join" list. Join match
rates come from Zetaris count queries, never an LLM confidence. Every
query id lands in the evidence record and the audit log.

## Meterless

The only door to models. The app talks to one OpenAI-compatible base URL
on the Meterless Runtime (Nightshift). Bearer token is read from
Nightshift's proxy-token file at runtime, never committed or logged.
Engines: Scout Intent signs every export, H-MEM with TrustLedger links
claims to fact ids and query ids, a minimal World Model tracks alert,
check-ins and network state.

## NVIDIA Nemotron

The only model family in the product. Join proposals, explanations, call
scripts, Content Safety, Parse and embeddings are Nemotron via NIM (cloud)
or local GGUF on the RTX 5080 through Meterless. No non-NVIDIA model runs
in the runtime path.

## Cursor

Cursor supplies the `.cursor/rules/` files: the rules every agent
(Cursor included) follows to stay inside its area, follow the house
rules and keep HANDOFF.md current. Cursor also runs the cloud agents
for the web UI seat and the data backup seat. The contract itself
(PR #14) was written by Devin, not by a Cursor run.
